      "answer": {
        "answer": "Landmark-grounded geography checkpoint completed and persisted as checkpoint:1cd738d4-a893-b3ce-4aee-e6805a0e70e5 at corpus revision generation:2999.",
        "claims": [
          {
            "id": "c1",
            "value": "Grand Basin is the broad basin immediately east of GRO \u201cMythic Cry,\u201d north of the active production corridor, with a large flat northern/northwestern pad. This supersedes the older provisional Red Lake/Redleaf match. Preserve a combat exclusion strip beside Mythic Cry\u2019s mountain/POI boundary, and keep the Geo Scanner near `3059,2618` outside the first build district.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Player save - sites and freight network.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c2",
            "value": "Flowworks is selected but not confirmed built. It lies between Landerworks and Faraday on a broad field with Titanium and Wolfram nearby and is intended to attach to their through trunk through one storage-yard spur. The dashed Landerworks\u2013Flowworks\u2013Faraday line records a relationship axis, not surveyed track geometry.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Player save - sites and freight network.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c3",
            "value": "Do not combine screenshot registration with SRDB coordinates unless a transform between those coordinate frames is verified. Preserve relational-only geography as relational: the Landerworks\u2013Flowworks\u2013Faraday line is not surveyed geometry, while Sunstone Station and Brimstone Utility have known parent relationships but no registered exact pins. Flowworks and Grand Basin are selected/planned rather than confirmed built.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Player save - sites and freight network.md",
              "Topics/StarRupture/StarRupture.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c4",
            "value": "The preferred first permanent Goethite source is the safer northwestern triple at approximately `1393\u20131464,1838\u20131891`, northwest of Mythic Cry/Grand Basin. After Engine access and Selenian 9, build all three Laser Drills, merge them into one Goethite-only Cargo Dispatcher, receive 45 raw Ore/min, and place one 1,600-unit Storage Depot v2 after the Receiver; this is preferred over the closer west field around `1252\u20131472,2950\u20133282`, which overlaps scanner/hostile envelopes. The preferred first Oil source is approximately `1234,3760`, west/southwest of Mythic Cry and Grand Basin. After Future Health 11, build one Oil Extractor and one Crude-only Dispatcher/Receiver pair, receive 10 Crude/min into one V2 buffer, and feed one GB-A Refinery. Reserve\u2014but do not initially build\u2014a second Oil pair and Refinery because one Refinery already consumes the full 10 Crude/min source plus large Titanium and Calcium feeds; the Oil marker around `1351,4473` is a separate site, not a same-pad extension. Goethite and Oil may share a receiver yard but must not share a Cargo link, rail lane, or storage unit.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Remote resource satellites - Goethite and Oil.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ],
        "checkpoint": {
          "objective": "Prepare a landmark-grounded geography handoff for Flowworks, corrected Grand Basin, and the first Goethite and Oil satellites without conflating coordinate frames or relational pins.",
          "current_state": [
            "Grand Basin\u2019s current canonical match is the basin immediately east of Mythic Cry; the provisional Red Lake/Redleaf match is superseded.",
            "Flowworks and Grand Basin remain selected/planned, not confirmed built.",
            "The first Goethite and Oil sources and their adopted raw-resource Cargo topology are documented.",
            "Checkpoint checkpoint:1cd738d4-a893-b3ce-4aee-e6805a0e70e5 was committed at generation:2999."
          ],
          "decisions": [
            "Use named landmarks and terrain relations before raw coordinates.",
